{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2026-09-26T22:07:10.253036+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-10T21:31:59.357714+00:00", "id": 22983513, "conceptrecid": "22983512", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22983513", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22983512", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22983513", "metadata": {"title": "Nonattainment in the Harrell\u2013Stubbe Dirichlet gap inequality", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22983513", "publication_date": "2026-09-23", "description": "<p>We prove that the universal Harrell\u2013Stubbe gap bound for Dirichlet eigenvalues is never attained on a nonempty bounded open subset of Euclidean space at any finite index. More strongly, Yang's first inequality is strict at every real threshold above the lowest eigenvalue. The proof uses the classical spectral remainder and a self-adjointness obstruction to finite spectral support of a coordinate times an eigenfunction. No boundary regularity or connectedness is required.</p><p>This answers the corrected saturation question recorded in the 2009 Oberwolfach report and listed as OWR-3389-016; the original report's missing square is explicitly documented. The package includes the paper, LaTeX source, independent AI-assisted proof audits, a scoped priority audit, and a dependency-free verifier with 7,016 exact checks. The computation checks algebra and box spectra, not the general analytic theorem. No earlier explicit nonattainment proof was located in the literature checked; this is not an exhaustive priority certification. Research and writing were AI-assisted.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": "Independent researcher", "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["spectral theory", "Dirichlet Laplacian", "Dirichlet eigenvalues", "universal eigenvalue inequalities", "Yang inequality", "Yang first inequality", "Harrell\u2013Stubbe inequality", "spectral gap", "eigenvalue gaps", "equality cases", "nonattainment", "commutator trace identities", "spectral remainder", "self-adjoint operators", "OWR-3389-016"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/tree/main/owr_3389_016_strict_gap", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://aleckriebel.github.io/Math/papers/strict-dirichlet-gap/", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.4171/OWR/2009/06", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1090/S0002-9947-97-01846-1", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/BF02829638", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "1.0.1", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22983512"}}]}, "notes": "Original manuscript and documentation: CC BY 4.0. Verification and build code: MIT (see LICENSES.md). No external peer-review or proof-assistant certification is claimed."}, "title": "Nonattainment in the Harrell\u2013Stubbe Dirichlet gap inequality", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22983513", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22983513", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22983513?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22983513", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22983513", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22983513", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22983513/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22983512", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22983512", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22983512", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22983512", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22983513/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22983513/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22